in Gryffindor&#x0201d;: Children&#x02019;s courage and its relationships to anxiety symptoms, Big Five personality traits, and sex roles (submitted).</citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muris</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Merckelbach</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ollendick</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bogie</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Three traditional and three new childhood anxiety questionnaires: Their reliability and validity in a normal adolescent sample</article-title><source>Behaviour Research and Therapy</source><year>2002</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>753</fpage><lpage>772</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0005-7967(01)00056-0</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Muris, P., Merckelbach, H., Ollendick, T. H., King, N. J., &#x00026; Bogie, N. (2002). Three traditional and three new childhood anxiety questionnaires: Their reliability and validity in a normal adolescent sample. Behaviour Research and Therapy,40, 753&#x02013;772. doi:10.1016/S0005-7967(01)00056-0. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12074371</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Norton</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The role of courage on behavioral approach in a fear-eliciting situation: A proof-of-concept pilot study</article-title><source>Journal of Anxiety Disorders</source><year>2009</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>212</fpage><lpage>217</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.janxdis.2008.07.002</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Norton, P. J., &#x00026; Weiss, B. J. (2009). The role of courage on behavioral approach in a fear-eliciting situation: A proof-of-concept pilot study. Journal of Anxiety Disorders,23, 212&#x02013;217. doi:10.1016/j.janxdis.2008.07.002. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18692986</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O&#x02019;Connor</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallam</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Rachman</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fearlessness and courage: A replication experiment</article-title><source>The British Journal of Psychology</source><year>1985</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>197</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">O&#x02019;Connor, K., Hallam, R. S., &#x00026; Rachman, S. J. (1985). Fearlessness and courage: A replication experiment. The British Journal of Psychology,76, 187&#x02013;197. </citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pury</surname><given-names>CLS</given-names></name><name><surname>Kowalski</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Spearman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distinctions between general and personal courage</article-title><source>Journal of Positive Psychology</source><year>2007</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>99</fpage><lpage>114</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/17439760701237962</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Pury, C. L. S., Kowalski, R. M., &#x00026; Spearman, J. (2007). Distinctions between general and personal courage. Journal of Positive Psychology,2, 99&#x02013;114. doi:10.1080/17439760701237962. </citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rachman</s